WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:08.096
I WANT TO SHARE SOME NOTES, SOME
EDITORIAL SUGGESTIONS THAT WERE

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:20.020
PREPARED AFTER THE SCREENING
OF A -- OF A MOVIE I WAS IN.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:23.480
OPENING TOO CHOPPY.

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.540
WHY IS THIS VOICEOVER
TRACK SO TERRIBLE?

00:00:27.255 --> 00:00:28.820
HE SOUNDS DRUGGED.

00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:31.760
WERE THEY ALL ON DRUGS?

00:00:32.518 --> 00:00:36.690
DECKARD AT THE PIANO
IS INTERMINABLE.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:38.980
FLASHBACK DIALOGUE CONFUSING.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.109
IS HE LISTENING TO A TAPE?

00:00:42.109 --> 00:00:46.059
WHY DO WE NEED THE
THIRD CUT TO THE EGGS?

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:50.429
THE SYNAGOGUE MUSIC
IS AWFUL ON THE STREET,

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:53.139
WE'VE GOT TO USE
VANGELIS.

00:00:53.139 --> 00:01:00.229
UP TO ZHORA'S DEATH, THE
MOVIE IS DEADLY DULL.

00:01:00.229 --> 00:01:03.704
THIS MOVIE GETS WORSE
EVERY SCREENING.

00:01:03.704 --> 00:01:06.484
[ LAUGHTER ]

00:01:08.310 --> 00:01:11.280
THAT MOVIE WAS CALLED
"BLADE RUNNER.”

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.270
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:01:18.136 --> 00:01:21.840
AND THESE NOTES CAN HELP US
UNDERSTAND WHY THE EDITING

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:26.773
PROCESS CAN OFTEN
GET A LITTLE COMPLICATED.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:33.920
THE POSSIBILITIES MAY SEEM
ENDLESS, BUT THE EDITOR WILL WORK

00:01:34.462 --> 00:01:41.929
TIRELESSLY, OFTEN IN ISOLATION,
TO MAKE THOUSANDS OF CHOICES

00:01:41.929 --> 00:01:46.909
PLACING THE RIGHT PIECE OF THE
RIGHT LENGTH IN THE RIGHT ORDER

00:01:46.909 --> 00:01:53.390
TO ARRIVE AT THE BEST VERSION OF
WHAT THE MOVIE WANTS TO BE.

00:01:54.639 --> 00:02:00.409
IT'S AN EXTREMELY DIFFICULT
PROCESS, NOT FOR THE IMPATIENT

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:02.270
NOT FOR THE FAINT OF HEART.

00:02:03.097 --> 00:02:07.109
YOU'VE GOT TO REALLY
LOVE MAKING MOVIES.

00:02:07.109 --> 00:02:10.810
TONIGHT'S NOMINEES FOR
BEST FILM EDITING ARE --

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:16.801
"THE FATHER,"
YORGOS LAMPRINOS.

00:02:16.801 --> 00:02:19.892
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:19.892 --> 00:02:24.181
"NOMADLAND,"
CHLOE ZHAO.

00:02:24.181 --> 00:02:26.569
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:30.660
"PROMISING YOUNG WOMAN,"
FREDERIC THORAVAL.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.572
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:39.647
"SOUND OF METAL,"
MIKKEL E.G. NIELSEN.

00:02:39.647 --> 00:02:42.379
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:42.379 --> 00:02:45.750
AND "THE TRIAL OF THE
CHICAGO 7," ALAN BAUMGARTEN.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:48.997
[ APPLAUSE ]

00:02:48.997 --> 00:02:51.010
AND THE OSCAR GOES TO --

00:02:53.387 --> 00:02:55.564
"SOUND OF METAL"

00:02:55.564 --> 00:02:57.848
MIKKEL E.G. NIELSEN.

00:02:57.848 --> 00:03:03.040
[ CHEERS AND APPLAUSE ]

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.189
THANK YOU,
THANK YOU ACADEMY.

00:03:35.189 --> 00:03:40.640
AND FELLOW NOMINEES,
YOU’RE AN INSPIRATION TO ME.

00:03:41.264 --> 00:03:45.519
I’M FROM DENMARK,
AND I WOULD LIKE TO

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:48.879
GREET DENMARK BECAUSE
THEY ARE EXTREMELY

00:03:48.879 --> 00:03:54.909
BOLD AT FUNDING
THE DANISH FILM SCHOOL

00:03:54.909 --> 00:03:57.970
SO WE STUDENTS CAN
DEVELOP OUR CRAFT AND

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.950
LANGUAGE FOR FOUR YEARS.

00:04:00.622 --> 00:04:01.709
IT’S AMAZING.

00:04:01.709 --> 00:04:05.490
THIS IS WHAT YOU GET, SO
JUST CONTINUE DOING IT.

00:04:07.169 --> 00:04:11.700
I WOULD LIKE TO THANK
EVE AND ANGUS

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:15.060
AND MY AMAZING
ASSISTANT ALEX.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:18.000
AND MY WHOLE FAMILY AT
ROCK PAPER SCISSORS.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:20.830
YOU GUYS RAISED THE BAR.

00:04:20.830 --> 00:04:26.610
I WOULD LIKE TO THANK
MY AGENTS, HILLARY AND REBECCA.

00:04:26.610 --> 00:04:30.630
I WOULD LIKE TO THANK
AMAZON AND CAVIAR

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.390
AND EVERYONE FROM
CAST AND CREW FOR SHARING

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:37.100
YOUR ENORMOUS TALENTS.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:40.890
THE DEAF COMMUNITY
FOR INVITING ME IN

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:45.720
VERY INSPIRING AND
REWARDING WORLDS.

00:04:45.720 --> 00:04:49.434
I WOULD LIKE TO THANK 
ALL MY FRIENDS, MY FAMILIES,

00:04:49.865 --> 00:04:54.040
MY PARENTS, I HAVE TO 
REMEMBER MY PARENTS.

00:04:54.040 --> 00:04:59.980
MY SISTERS, MY WIFE JUDITH
AND MY KIDS MINGUS AND ELLA.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:02.100
THEY ALWAYS ALLOW ME
TO SPEND TIME WITH

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:04.030
MY BIG LOVE AFFAIR:
EDITING.

00:05:04.030 --> 00:05:07.150
SO THANK YOU FOR THAT.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:09.560
BUT ONE ABOVE ALL,

00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:12.380
DARIUS MARDER.

00:05:12.380 --> 00:05:16.190
THANK YOU FOR YOUR
INCREDIBLE VISION.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.580
THANK YOU FOR INVITING ME
ON THIS LIFE-CHANGING,

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:25.410
I WOULD SAY, JOURNEY.
AND IT’S BEEN LIKE FOLLOWING

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:28.610
A RAINBOW FOR ME
AND TODAY I FEEL LIKE

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.190
WE FOUND THE GOLD.

00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:31.410
THANK YOU.

